{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0013400","label":"Congenital adrenal insufficiency with 46, XY sex reversal OR 46,XY disorder of sex development-adrenal insufficiency due to CYP11A1 deficiency","definition":"A rare, genetic, developmental defect during embryogenesis disorder characterized by severe, early-onset, salt-wasting adrenal insufficiency and ambiguous/female external genitalia (irrespective of chromosomal sex) due to mutations in the <i>CYP11A1</i> gene. Milder cases may present delayed onset of adrenal gland dysfunction and genitalia phenotype may range from normal male to female in individuals with 46,XY karyotype. Imaging studies reveal hypoplastic/absent adrenal glands and biochemical findings include low serum cortisol, mineralocorticoids, androgens, and sodium, with elevated potassium levels.","synonyms":["XY sex reversal-adrenal failure","XY sex reversal-adrenal failure syndrome","adrenal insufficiency, congenital, with 46,XY SEX reversal, partial or complete","adrenal insufficiency, congenital, with 46XY sex reversal, partial or complete","cholesterol side-chain cleavage deficiency","p450scc deficiency"],"xrefs":["DOID:0050546","GARD:0017033","MEDGEN:462405","MESH:C566130","NCIT:C131422","OMIM:613743","Orphanet:168558","UMLS:C3151055"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":4,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":54,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_5c54af0e5e10","source":"MONDO:0013400","target":"CYP11A1","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:168558","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/168558","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (loss of function) in (Assessed) — cytochrome P450 family 11 subfamily A member 1"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:168558","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPH